QuestGuidance.Register("en",225,{
[7169]="7000B24D\n1\tTalk to Basil Gummidge\tBasil Gummidge has travelled with you to the Sparring Circle of Ost Forod. Basil Gummidge is waiting to speak with you inside the Sparring Circle.\n2\tDefeat Cuthbert Sprunt\tYou are engaged in single combat with Cuthbert Sprunt in the Sparring Circle. Basil Gummidge is overseeing the combat to ensure that Cuthbert does not cheat.\n3\tDefeat Cuthbert Sprunt\tCuthbert Sprunt has revealed his true colours and has called upon his cronies for aid. Basil Gummidge has leapt to your defence, and with his aid, you must defeat the enemy.\n4\tTalk to Basil Gummidge\tBasil Gummidge is in the Sparring Circle of Ost Forod. You and Basil Gummidge have successfully overcome Cuthbert Sprunt's treachery. You should speak with Basil at once.\n",
[7170]="70049F33\n1\tTalk to Glorfindel\tGlorfindel waits for you to approach the council.\n2\tApproach the Council\tIt is time to approach the Council of War.\n3\tTalk to Glorfindel\tYou and Glorfindel have joined the Council of War. Talk to him to hear of the text he recovered.\n4\tTalk to Galadriel\tHear what Galadriel has to say of the prophecy.\n5\tHear Galadriel's pronouncement\tGaladriel will now address the Council of War.\n",
[7171]="7002FA0D\n1\tTalk to Aragorn by the camp-fire\tAragorn is by the camp-fire on Parth Galen.\n2\tTalk to the Elf, Legolas, by the camp-fire\tThe Elf, Legolas, is by the camp-fire.\n3\tFind Frodo and convince him to bring the Ring to Minas Tirith. He wandered somewhere to the north-west.\tYour companions do not understand. You have to find Frodo and make him understand that the Ring must go to Minas Tirith.\n4\tTalk to Frodo and see if he has yet decided what to do\tFrodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring.\n5\tTalk to Frodo and tell him of Minas Tirith's great need\tFrodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring.\n6\tTalk to Frodo and ask to borrow the Ring so you can save Gondor\tFrodo has wandered partially up Amon Hen. He needs to be told of your city's great need for the Ring. Perhaps he will lend it to you? You can use the Ring to save Minas Tirith, and all of Gondor!\n7\tSeize the Ring from Frodo!\tFrodo will doom us all! You have to take the Ring from him before he ransoms Middle-earth to Sauron!\n8\tSearch the hollow log for the sneaking hobbit!\030Search the leaf pile for the sneaking hobbit!\030Search through the bush for the sneaking hobbit!\tThe sneak must be hiding somewhere around here! Search the places he might be hiding, and seize the Ring!\n9\tFrodo is gone. You should return to the camp-site and see if he will forgive your outburst\tFrodo is gone, and the anger has lifted from your senses much as a cloud moves on from covering the sun. You should return now to Aragorn and the rest of your party. Perhaps Frodo has returned to them and will forgive you your outburst.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn wants to know where you have been.\n",
[7172]="700375DD\n1\tTalk to Thane Torferth\tThane Torferth stands on the road to Stoke. You should speak with Thane Torferth before the attack.\n2\tFight through Ordlac's forces to the Mead Hall of Stoke\tThe Mead Hall of Stoke is at the end of the road. Torferth is making for the Mead Hall of Stoke, where he intends to confront Ordlac.\n3\tDefeat Dudsig and his guards\030Talk to Thane Torferth\tDudsig and his guards are blocking the way to Ordlac and the children. Defeat them and confront Ordlac.\n4\tDefeat Ordlac and protect the children\tOrdlac is near the end of the Mead Hall, threatening Reeve Fríthild's children. Aid Torferth against Ordlac and protect the children.\n5\tTalk to Thane Torferth\tThane Torferth is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should speak with Thane Torferth at once.\n",
[7173]="7006EF58\n1\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax rests on a cot by the entrance of the cage.\n2\tPass the time in your cage\tIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.\n3\tListen to the words of your visitor\tIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.\n4\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax rests on a cot by the entrance of the cage.\n5\tListen to the words of your captor\tYour captor stands outside the cage for some purpose of her own.\n6\tTalk to your captor through the bars of your cage\tYour captor stands outside the cage for some purpose of her own.\n7\tPass the time in your cage\tIt is difficult to measure the passing of time in the cage.\n8\tBeckon the girl to speak\tPerhaps if you beckon the girl she will speak to you.\n9\tWait for the girl to speak\tThe girl eyes you warily.\n10\tTalk to the mysterious girl\tThe girl eyes you warily.\n11\tTalk to the mysterious girl\tThe girl eyes you warily.\n12\tGive Tephísa your answer\tTephísa waits for your response.\n13\tWait to see what she will do\tYou have given your answer, and must now wait to see her response.\n14\tSee what Jajax thinks\tThere is nothing more you can do but wait.\n",
[7174]="70027AD2\n1\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in the prison-caves\tLheu Brenin has come with you into the prison-caves behind Tûr Morva to speak with the captive emissary.\n2\tTalk to Léolin in the prison-caves\tLéolin is waiting to speak with you in the prison-caves.\n3\tTalk to Lothrandir in the prison-caves\tYou have met Lothrandir in the prison-caves, coming back from an errand in the depths.\n4\tTalk to Nai in the prison-caves\tNai is guarding the cell where Dondhreg is being held captive in the prison-caves.\n5\tTalk to Lothrandir in the prison-caves\tBetrayal... you were attacked by two members of the Falcon-clan, but Lothrandir was able to turn the tables on them. You should speak with him now.\n6\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in the prison-caves\tLheu Brenin has blocked your passage with a group of armed warriors. He wishes to speak with you.\n7\tSurvive the waggon ride along a bumpy road\tYou have been brought to Isengard by waggon along a bumpy road.\n8\tTalk to Iwan at the gate into Isengard\tIwan is ready to bring you into Isengard.\n9\tTalk to Lothrandir at the gates of Isengard\tLothrandir has been badly beaten by your captors and is finding it difficult to go on.\n10\tFollow Lothrandir into Isengard\tLothrandir is running into the heart of Isengard by his own power. It is a small gesture, but it is something, and gives you a glimmer of hope.\n11\tTalk to Morflak in Isengard\tAn Uruk-hai named Morflak has made you pull up short before the tower of Orthanc.\n",
[7175]="70031778\n1\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling is standing with the crofters at The Raided Crofts. Having made it this far, Gísling has asked for your aid in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn.\n2\tEscort the crofters of Garsfeld to safety\tGísling is walking with the crofters along the road south to Snowbourn. Gísling hopes you can aid him in escorting the crofters of Garsfeld to Snowbourn. However, he fears that Orcs lurk just beyond his sight and threaten to harm his people.\n3\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling can be found along the road to Snowbourn.\n",
[7176]="7004A8D9\n1\tRescue Mr. Frodo from the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tMr. Frodo can be found somewhere in the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\n2\tSee what could be if you were only to claim the Ring!\tThe Ring has begun to tempt you! You must resist and rescue Mr. Frodo.\n3\tUse your hobbit-sense\tThe Ring has tempted you with visions of yourself as Samwise the Strong. Use your hobbit-sense, Sam! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tPass through the gate of Cirith Ungol\tThe gate of Cirith Ungol can be found at the easternmost point of Cirith Ungol.\n5\tHarden your will and charge at the gate of Cirith Ungol!\tAn unseen force seems to block your passage into Cirith Ungol.\n6\tDraw the phial of Galadriel and hold it aloft!\tThe phial of Galadriel! Its light might overcome whatever force bars your path!\n7\tSpring past the Silent Watchers into Cirith Ungol!\tNow's your chance! Mr. Frodo needs your help!\n8\tSearch for Mr. Frodo in the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tMr. Frodo can be found somewhere in the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\n9\tAscend the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tAn Orc has fled from you. You should continue higher into the Tower of Cirith Ungol in search of Mr. Frodo.\n10\tHide behind slain Orcs and wreckage!\tYou hear Orkish voices, and the familiar voice of Shagrat. Quickly, hide!\n11\tWait for the right moment\tShagrat has chased the Orc, Snaga, onto the parapet of Cirith Ungol. You should remain hidden until the right moment.\n12\tConfront Shagrat\tShagrat is blocking your path into the heights of Cirith Ungol. It's now or never, Sam!\n13\tFind the topmost chamber of Cirith Ungol\tMr. Frodo must be in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Keep climbing!\n14\tRescue Mr. Frodo from the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tMr. Frodo must be in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol, and it sounds like he's in danger!\n15\tTalk to Mr. Frodo and escape the Tower of Cirith Ungol\tYou've rescued Mr. Frodo!\n",
[7177]="700162B4\n1\tUse the summoning horn to call Slagvi\tA summoning horn stands at the front of the cooling chamber. The summoning horn can be used to call Slagvi to your side.\n2\tTalk to Slagvi\tSlagvi is at your side in the cooling chamber. You should speak with Slagvi.\n3\tFind and defeat the Moria chieftain\tSlagvi wants the goblin-leader who has claimed the cooling chamber found and defeated.\n4\tFix the jammed lever\030Repair the rusted gear\030Repair the stuck wheel\tThe items to repair can be found at the back of the cooling chamber.\n5\tTalk to Slagvi\tTalk to Slagvi. You can summon him if you become separated.\n6\tExit the cooling chamber\tIt is time to exit the cooling chamber.\n",
[7178]="7002CC3C\n1\tTalk to Doron\tDoron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant, after having patrolled the road down to the Limlight with his men.\n2\tDoron is stationed outside of Ost Celebrant. You should follow him as he tells his tale.\t\n3\tFollow Doron into Ost Celebrant\tHaving survived an Easterling assault, Doron is entering Ost Celebrant, where he hopes to reunite with the rest of his men.\n4\tFollow Doron into Ost Celebrant\tDoron is inside Ost Celebrant with his men. You should listen as he continues his tale.\n5\tFollow Doron outside Ost Celebrant\tHaving heard the roar of an approaching force, Doron and his men have decided to cross the bridge of Ost Celebrant and confront the invaders.\n6\tTalk to Doron\tDoron is standing on the edge of the bridge into Ost Celebrant.\n",
[7179]="70021CE0\n1\tTalk to Dufrig\tSpeak with Dufrig before the Council of Brehur begins.\n2\tObserve the deliberations of the Council\tObserve the deliberations of the Council.\n3\tPlace the sword before the brenin\030Place the helm before the brenin\tBring forward the items you found upon the half-orc raiders as evidence of Isengard's involvement in the attacks.\n4\tObserve the deliberations of the Council\tObserve the deliberations of the Council.\n5\tDefeat the Champion of Isengard\tDefeat the Champion of Isengard.\n6\tTalk to Glynn Brenin\tSpeak with Glynn Brenin regarding the emissary from Isengard.\n",
[7180]="70038033\n1\tTalk to Herubrand\tHerubrand's council is meeting in the cellar of the farmhouse, and Herubrand has invited you to join them.\n2\tObserve the council meeting\tHerubrand's council is meeting in the cellar of the farmhouse, and Herubrand has invited you to join them.\n",
[7181]="700539E4\n1\tTalk to Tárandil\tTárandil is outside the pavilion where the council of the kings will take place.\n2\tWait for the council of the kings to begin\tThe council of the kings will soon begin, and the sons of Isildur are hopeful that their presence and yours will go unremarked.\n3\tTalk to High King Gil-galad\tHigh King Gil-galad has reservations about your attendance and that of Isildur's sons.\n4\tObserve the council of the kings\tHigh King Gil-galad has called into question your presence, and that of the sons of Isildur, at the council of kings.\n5\tTalk to Vëamacil\tVëamacil is in the tent where the council of kings is underway.\n6\tObserve the council of the kings\tThe council of kings is underway.\n7\tTalk to Vëamacil\tLendelen of the Bright Company has proposed a dangerous plan by which Sauron's hold over the Ghâzab Bôron might be broken.\n8\tObserve the council of the kings\tThe council of the kings continues, but not all in attendance are satisfied with its pronouncements.\n9\tTalk to High King Elendil\tHigh King Elendil is inside the pavilion for the council of kings.\n",
[7182]="700374A6\n1\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tSpeak with Reeve Fríthild.\n2\tObserve the Council of Stoke\tObserve the Council of Stoke.\n3\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tSpeak with Reeve Fríthild.\n4\tCollect Fríthild's mail\030Collect Fríthild's shield\030Collect Fríthild's sword\tReeve Fríthild's sword, shield, and mail are on the table below the dais. Reeve Fríthild asked you to collect her arms and armour.\n5\tBring the sword, shield, and mail to Reeve Fríthild\tBring the sword, shield, and mail to Reeve Fríthild.\n6\tTalk to Reeve Fríthild\tSpeak with Reeve Fríthild.\n",
[7183]="700467C6\n1\tTalk to Aragorn inside the pavilion\tAragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir inside the pavilion\tMithrandir is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.\n3\tTalk to Imrahil in the pavilion\tPrince Imrahil is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.\n4\tObserve the council of the captains\tAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.\n5\tTalk to Mithrandir inside the pavilion\tMithrandir is holding council inside Aragorn's pavilion on the Pelennor.\n6\tObserve the council of the captains\tAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.\n7\tTalk to Aragorn inside the pavilion\tAragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.\n8\tObserve the council of the captains\tAragorn and the captains of the armies are meeting to decide their next course.\n9\tTalk to Aragorn inside the pavilion\tAragorn is inside his pavilion with many of the captains who fought at Pelennor.\n",
[7184]="70048BFF\n1\tTalk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n2\tListen to Annoth's account of the Thandrim\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n3\tTalk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n4\tListen to Annoth's account of the Thandrim\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n5\tTalk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n6\tListen to Annoth's account of the Thandrim\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n7\tTalk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n8\tListen to Annoth's account of the Thandrim\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n9\tTalk to Annoth during his recounting of the tale\tIt is important to Annoth that you hear the tale of the Thandrim.\n",
[7185]="70040431\n1\tTalk to Rosfin\tRosfin can be found beside the fireplace in Malthellam's home. You have come to tell Malthellam and Rosfin of what you have learned of the Dead and Tarlang's Crown. You should speak to Rosfin while you wait for Malthellam.\n2\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found beside the fireplace in his home. You have come to tell Malthellam and Rosfin of what you have learned of the Dead and Tarlang's Crown. You should speak to Malthellam.\n3\tListen to Malthellam\tMalthellam and Rosfin are speaking in Malthellam's home. You have informed them that the Dead continue to haunt the vale.\n4\tRecount your story to Malthellam and Rosfin\tMalthellam is near his fireplace in his home. Malthellam and Rosfin spoke at length on the history of the vale, and Malthellam now desires to hear the rest of your tale.\n5\tListen to Malthellam and Rosfin\tMalthellam and Rosfin are speaking in Malthellam's home. You have told them of all that you experiencing in Alagrant and Sardol, and now Malthellam and Rosfin are discussing what is to be done.\n6\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found beside the fireplace in his home. You have finished discussing matters with Rosfin and Malthellam and should speak to Malthellam once more before readying yourself to journey into the vale once more.\n",
[7186]="7002AD6C\n1\tTalk to Théodred on the eyot in the Isen\tThéodred is waiting to speak with you on the eyot in the middle of the Isen. It is dawn and nearly time to begin the daring strike on Isengard. Théodred is waiting to speak with you before his host rides north.\n2\tTalk to Théodred on the eyot in the Isen\tThéodred has given Cynstan a message to deliver and is waiting to speak with you again.\n3\tTalk to Cynstan on the eyot in the Isen\tCynstan is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen.\n4\tTalk to Cynstan in the middle of the Ford\tCynstan is in the middle of the Ford. He is concerned about something and wants to speak with you.\n5\tTalk to Cadda on the east bank of the river Isen\tCadda is on the east bank of the Ford, and he wants to speak with you.\n6\tTalk to Cynstan on the east bank of the Isen\tCynstan is on the east bank of the river Isen and wants to talk to you.\n7\tCross the Ford of Isen once more and speak with Théodred on the eyot\tThéodred is on the eyot in the middle of the river Isen. Cynstan has asked you to tell him that the Ford will be in Cadda's capable hands while the Prince rides to Isengard.\n8\tMount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to ride\tThéodred has asked you to mount your steed and talk to Grimbold when you are ready to ride to Isengard.\n9\tTravel up the road to Isengard\tYou have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host.\n10\tTalk to Grimbold on the road to Isengard\tYou have travelled up the road towards Isengard with the host, and Grimbold wants to speak with you.\n11\tTalk to Théodred on the road to Isengard\tYou have come part of the way up the road to Isengard, and now Théodred is waiting for the return of his scout. You should speak with the Prince.\n12\tTalk to Théodred on the road to Isengard\tThe scout has returned from Isengard and brings word to Théodred that the number of Orcs and half-orcs outside the walls is not to be feared. Théodred wants to discuss this report with you.\n",
[7187]="7002AD6D\n1\tTalk to Théodred\tThéodred is waiting to address his assembled men, and you should speak with him.\n2\tTalk to Grimbold at the head of the host\tPrince Théodred has asked you and Grimbold to cut through the brush on the eastern side of the road to attack the half-orc flank.\n3\tTalk to Rungar\tRungar has arrived on the flank of the main host, and you should speak with him.\n4\tTalk to Grimbold before the gates of Isengard\tBefore the gates of Isengard, the Rohirrim led by Théodred have come under attack by an overwhelming force of Saruman's uruks. You need to speak with Grimbold amid the chaos of battle!\n5\tDefeat netted uruk-warriors at the gates of Isengard (total: 3)\tThe riders have netted some of the attacking uruks, and Grimbold has charged you with defeating them in order to buy time for the retreat.\n",
[7188]="700442C0\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir before the broken gate\tYou have hurried down to the ruin of the gates with Mithrandir. Only he can stand against the Witch-king.\n2\tWitness the confrontation between Mithrandir and the Witch-king of Angmar\tMithrandir stands alone before the Witch-king, blocking his passage into the city.\n3\tEscape from the enemy and find Peregrin Took\tYou must find Peregrin Took and protect him from the forces of the Enemy!\n4\tEscape from the enemy and find Peregrin Took\tYou must find Peregrin Took and protect him from the forces of the Enemy!\n5\tEscape from the enemy and find Peregrin Took\tYou must find Peregrin Took and protect him from the forces of the Enemy!\n6\tTalk to Imrahil\tImrahil has slain many Orcs, and has called to you for news of the gate.\n7\tWait for a chance to turn the tables on your captors\tYou have been captured by the Enemy!\n8\tTalk to Gothmog atop the city\tGothmog stands before you at the top of the city, secure in victory.\n9\tFight alongside Denethor atop the city\tDenethor has emerged from the tower, ready to die for his city and his people.\n10\tTalk to Denethor before he succumbs to his wounds\tDenethor has been wounded.\n11\tRemain alert for any chance to help Peregrin or Denethor!\tPeregrin Took is in grave danger!\n12\tTalk to Denethor amid the terrible visions\tYour mind is filled with terrible visions, but the voice of the Steward cuts through the frightening images.\n13\tYour mind is full of hazy, troubled images\tYour mind is filled with terrible visions, but the voice of the Steward cuts through the frightening images.\n14\tShake off your reverie, and talk to Denethor\tDenethor is standing before you, his face an earnest mask of despair and hopelessness.\n",
[7189]="700346E2\n1\tAsk Ludeca about the snow\tYou have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.\n2\tListen to your neighbours\tYou have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.\n3\tTalk to Ludeca\tYou have come outside of your home in town to find the snow worse than any weather you have seen in this part of Rohan.\n4\tSearch near the windmill for the source of the rumbling\tThe rumbling came from north-west of town. You should search for the source of the rumbling.\n5\tTell Ludeca of the terrible force north-west of Dunfast\tLudeca is in Dunfast. You should speak with Ludeca.\n6\tSomething evil bears down on Dunfast. You should ensure that everyone has evacuated their homes.\t\n7\tBreak the lock to Forthere's home\tForthere's house is on the outskirts of Dunfast. You should break into Forthere's house.\n8\tConvince Forthere to evacuate\tForthere is in his home in Dunfast. You should convince Forthere to evacuate immediately.\n",
[7190]="7006F2BF\n1\tTalk to Ulishár in the audience\tUlishár eagerly waits for the play to begin in the city of Zajâna.\n2\tWatch the performance\tWhile the performance continues, you should remain a model audience member.\n3\tTalk to Inkanûsh in the audience\tSomething has captured Inkanûsh's attention.\n4\tWatch the performance\tWhile the performance continues, you should remain a model audience member.\n5\tTalk to Ulishár in the audience\tUlishár enjoyed the performance, but his expression is one of worry.\n",
[7191]="7004D6EA\n1\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun has been waiting for you. You should talk to Dagrun.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n3\tTalk to Dagrun\tHoskuld ran into the kitchen, seeming unwell. You should talk to Dagrun.\n4\tCheck on Hoskuld\tHoskuld ran into the kitchen, seemingly unwell. You should check on Hoskuld.\n5\tTalk to Dagrun\tHoskuld is dead! You should talk to Dagrun!\n6\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n7\tFind Háta\tHáta did not return with the others. You should find Háta.\n8\tTalk to Dagrun\tHáta is dead! You should talk to Dagrun!\n9\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n10\tTalk to Dagrun\tThe dinner guests have all split up. You should talk to Dagrun.\n11\tCheck on Maeriel\tMaeriel has left the room, angered at the other guests' behaviour. You should go check on Maeriel.\n12\tTalk to Dagrun\tMaeriel is dead! You should talk to Dagrun!\n13\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n14\tCheck on Thewár\tThewár has suddenly fallen down the stairs! You should check on Thewár!\n15\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n16\tTalk to Dagrun\tThewár is dead! You should talk to Dagrun!\n17\tFind the source of the crash\tA loud crash came from upstairs. You should find the source of the crash.\n18\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n19\tTalk to Captain Álarr\tCaptain Álarr has arrived downstairs. You should talk to Álarr.\n20\tAccuse someone of murder!\tYou must accuse someone of murder! Choose wisely!\n21\tListen to the conversation\tThe dinner guests are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n22\tTalk to Rikolf the Elder\tRikolf the Elder wants to speak with you. You should talk to Rikolf the Elder.\n23\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun has been named Master! You should talk to Dagrun.\n",
[7192]="700582CE\n1\tApproach the vision of Karazgar and Fram\tApproach the vision of Karazgar and Fram.\n2\tExperience the vision\tExperience the vision. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[7193]="7004319C\n1\tTalk to Baranor\tBaranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep. The Haradrim are likely to attack soon. Talk to Baranor now.\n2\tDefend Arnach\tBaranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep. Defend the keep with Baranor and his men.\n3\tTalk to Baranor\tBaranor stands on the bridge before Arnach's keep. The Haradrim assault has be deflected. Baranor waits to talk with you.\n",
[7194]="7003049F\n1\tDefend Faldham with the help of Thane Elfmar\tElfmar remains ready, just north of the road fork at the north edge of Faldham. The defence against the White Hand forces has begun, and Thane Elfmar seems both confident and prepared.\n2\tSpeak to Thane Elfmar\tElfmar remains ready, just north of the road fork at the north edge of Faldham. Thane Elfmar wishes to speak with you about the defences of Faldham.\n3\tSpeak to Nothwulf along the road to the south-west\tNothwulf can be found to the south-west, along the road near the southern farms. Elfmar has asked you to aid Nothwulf defend the southern perimeter.\n4\tRide with Nothwulf to defend the southern perimeter\tNothwulf can be found to the south-west, along the road near the southern farms. Nothwulf will need your aid to defend the southern perimeter.\n5\tSpeak with Nothwulf about the defences\tNothwulf awaits at the southern edge of Faldham. Nothwulf wishes to speak about the ongoing defence of the town.\n6\tRide with Osin to defend the south-west edge of Faldham\tOsin has approached Nothwulf from the west\n7\tSpeak to Langfrith guarding the mead hall gates\tLangfrith defends the gate to the mead hall of Faldham. Langfrith has been guarding the mead hall entrance, and Osin believes that he may need your assistance.\n8\tDefeat Urbhár, the Orc commander\030Defeat Botglim, the Uruk commander\tUrbhár and Botglim can be found north of the mead hall. Langfrith believes that defeating the commanders of the invaders, Urbhár and Botglim, may disrupt the ongoing assault.\n9\tSpeak to Thane Elfmar at the mead hall gates\tElfmar and members of the Elfward await at the opening to the mead hall of Faldham. Elfmar and the Elfward must be notified that you have defeated the commanders of the attacking army.\n",
[7195]="70029F54\n1\tTalk to Bron\tYou should talk to Bron.\n2\tDefeat the Uruk-hai master and his forces\tDefend Galtrev from the White Hand forces.\n3\tTalk to Bron\tBron is in Galtrev.\n",
[7196]="70001808\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tAid Halbarad in the defence of Trestlebridge.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad stands on the Trestlebridge, near Nellie Boskins. Alongside Halbarad and the people of Trestlebridge, you have defended the town against the Ongbúrz Orcs.\n",
[7197]="7000E7A5\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tAid Halbarad in the defence of Trestlebridge.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad stands on the Trestlebridge, near Nellie Boskins. Alongside Halbarad and the people of Trestlebridge, you have defended the town against the Ongbúrz Orcs.\n",
[7198]="70053B30\n1\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n2\tHear the words of Vëamacil as remembered by Vágari\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n3\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n4\tHear the words of Meldaran as remembered by Vágari\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n5\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n6\tFind some sign that Isildur made for the river-bank\tVágari believed Isildur ran for the river-bank, and he desperately searched for some sign of the king's escape.\n7\tSwim across the river to find Isildur\tVágari believed Isildur attempted to swim across the river in order to escape.\n8\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n9\tListen to Vágari's account\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n10\tTalk to Tárandil\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n11\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer desires to speak to you of his past misdeeds.\n",
[7199]="70059A86\n1\tTalk to Muzmák in Durshulot\tMuzmák is waiting to speak with you.\n2\tTalk to Shulgolb\030Talk to Lumbag\030Talk to Zogmauk\tMuzmák gave you the names of three similar-minded residents of Durshulot who might help you escape from the growing conflict beneath Gundabad.\n3\tTalk to Muzmák in Durshulot\tMuzmák is waiting to speak with you.\n4\tRemain alert during Gorgar's inspection\tAn unexpected visitor has interrupted your plans.\n5\tTalk to Gorgar the Ruthless\tGorgar has chosen you for some unknown purpose.\n6\tCarry out Gorgar's plan\tGorgar has need of a goblin to acquire a valuable treasure for him.\n7\tCollect the mithril treasure sought by Gorgar\tGorgar believes there is a mithril treasure in the room on this side of the rock-fall.\n8\tContinue working for Gorgar\tAcquiring the mithril hammer for Gorgar was only the beginning.\n9\tCommand Ránulur to fight on behalf of Gorgar\tGorgar the Ruthless has sent you to command the loyalty of Ránulur, Chieftain of Wargs.\n10\tCarry out the wishes of Gorgar the Ruthless\tYou served Gorgar faithfully and well.\n11\tTalk to Muzmák during the War of Three Peaks\tThe War of Three Peaks is underway!\n12\tContinue your flight from the war\tYou ran far from the battle-lines, eventually finding yourself on distant snowfields.\n13\tTalk to Muzmák as he catches his breath\tYou have run with Muzmák from the War of Three Peaks... but how far will be enough?\n14\tSurvive the reemergence of Hrímil Frost-heart\tHrímil Frost-heart has emerged from her icy prison behind the Anvil of Winterstith!\n15\tTalk to Muzmák\tMuzmák stands in silence upon the snowfield.\n",
[7200]="70010045\n1\tFind Amarthiel somewhere within Tham Mírdain\tYou must find Amarthiel before she can reforge Narchuil.\n2\tTalk to Laerdan\tYou have found Laerdan lying within the entrance to Tham Mírdain, gravely wounded. You should learn from him what happened.\n3\tDefeat the doorwarden, Strok\tLaerdan instructed you to find and defeat the Gorthorog Strok, who bears the keys to Tham Mírdain.\n4\tEnter Tham Mírdain\tYou should use the keys you recovered from Strok to gain entry into Tham Mírdain.\n5\tFind the ring-forges of Tham Mírdain\tYou must find the ring-forges of Tham Mírdain.\n6\tConfront Amarthiel\tYou must confront Amarthiel at the ring-forges of Tham Mírdain.\n7\tFollow Amarthiel and Mordrambor\tAmarthiel was interrupted by the arrival of the Black Númenórean Mordrambor. You should follow them to learn what new evil has arisen.\n",
})
